      "math_academy_id": "q-40558",
      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{36}\\cdot \\sqrt{48}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{6\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{3\\sqrt{3}})≈{15.79}^{∘}.\n$$",
